                <pb facs="0195" n="1029" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1029"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/8921</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-22T14:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 22, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4706, For McFadden [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 144. Stetson. Embassy’s 4093, June 5, 6 p.m. Your 154. On April 30 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">29</hi>] War Trade Board passed resolution providing
                    that upon similar action being taken by the Governments of Great Britain,
                    France, and Italy committees may be constituted consisting of representatives of
                    each of above countries and the United States at Paris, London, and Washington
                    to recommend action to be taken upon all applications for licenses to trade with
                    enemy other than certain excepted classes. Committee in Paris to handle
                    transactions with persons in Spain, Morocco, and Switzerland. Committee in
                    London to handle transactions with persons in northern neutral countries.
                    Committee in Washington to handle transactions with persons resident in Western
                    Hemisphere. Now awaiting final approval of Great Britain to put plan in
                    operation. This has not been received in Washington as yet. When received, full
                    particulars, including instructions as to your course of action, will be sent
                    you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
